WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:02.370
- [Instructor] We are told
a teacher bought 12 sheets

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:05.300
of stickers to use on the
homework of her students.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:07.780
Each sheet had 48 stickers.

00:00:07.780 --> 00:00:09.070
At the end of the year,

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.520
the teacher had 123 stickers remaining.

00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:14.190
Which is the best estimate

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:17.270
for the number of
stickers the teacher used?

00:00:17.270 --> 00:00:19.700
So like always, pause this
video, and see if you can

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.520
have a go at this before
we work on this together.

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:24.360
All right, now let's
work on this together.

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:25.720
So the first thing to appreciate is

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:27.610
we just have to figure out an estimate.

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:29.800
We don't have to figure
out the exact number

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:32.940
of the stickers that were used.

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.940
Let's see if we can do that.

00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:36.230
So let's see,

00:00:36.230 --> 00:00:40.120
we have 12 sheets of stickers,

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:43.660
and each sheet had 48 stickers,

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:46.220
48 stickers per sheet.

00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:49.490
So how many stickers did
the teacher start off with?

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:52.690
Well, there were 12 sheets

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:57.690
times the number of stickers
per sheet, so times 48,

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.610
times 48.

00:00:59.610 --> 00:01:02.730
This is going to be the number
that they started off with,

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:05.850
number to start.

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:08.430
And then if we want to figure
out the number that are used,

00:01:08.430 --> 00:01:10.040
we just have to figure out, okay,

00:01:10.040 --> 00:01:12.870
from the number that was
started, how many are left over?

00:01:12.870 --> 00:01:15.260
And then that's how many were used.

00:01:15.260 --> 00:01:17.663
And so how many were left over?

00:01:17.663 --> 00:01:20.330
Well, 123 were remaining
at the end of the year,

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:22.690
so that's this number right over here.

00:01:22.690 --> 00:01:25.920
So if we calculate that
first, the number to start,

00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:29.050
we subtract out the
number that are remaining,

00:01:29.050 --> 00:01:32.710
then that will be equal
to the number of stickers

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:35.190
that the teacher used.

00:01:35.190 --> 00:01:37.040
Now once again, we don't
have to figure out exactly.

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:38.310
We just have to estimate.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:39.850
And so I'm just going to try

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:42.780
to figure out friendlier
numbers to work with.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:46.460
So instead of 12, let's imagine,

00:01:46.460 --> 00:01:48.370
let's imagine, actually,
I'll stick with 12.

00:01:48.370 --> 00:01:50.030
12 I can work with.

00:01:50.030 --> 00:01:51.270
But let's say that this is going

00:01:51.270 --> 00:01:54.090
to be approximately equal to,

00:01:54.090 --> 00:01:56.040
so in parentheses, instead of 48,

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.740
I'll say it's roughly 50.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:02:02.740
So this is going to be
approximately 12 times 50.

00:02:02.930 --> 00:02:06.740
Instead of 123, I'll say that's roughly,

00:02:06.740 --> 00:02:10.720
a friendlier number might
be 120 or might be 100.

00:02:10.720 --> 00:02:13.580
Let's just do 120, so minus 120.

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:14.750
We could've done 100.

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.450
And so we could figure out
what this is in our heads

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:18.900
or with a little bit of paper.

00:02:18.900 --> 00:02:23.480
12 times five is 60,
so 12 times 50 is 600.

00:02:23.480 --> 00:02:26.480
And then 600, if we had 100 here,

00:02:26.480 --> 00:02:28.620
600 minus 100 would've been 500,

00:02:28.620 --> 00:02:31.240
or 600 minus 120 is 480.

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:33.130
So what we want to do
is look at the choice

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:35.610
and see which of these choices is closest

00:02:35.610 --> 00:02:39.230
to roughly 500 or roughly 480?

00:02:39.230 --> 00:02:42.050
And so let's see, out of all of these,

00:02:42.050 --> 00:02:45.030
actually they have exactly 480, which is,

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:47.670
so they estimated exactly the
way we happened to estimate.

00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:49.600
Now not every person is going to do that.

00:02:49.600 --> 00:02:50.940
We could've chosen,

00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.930
instead of 123 becoming
120 in our estimate,

00:02:53.930 --> 00:02:57.010
we could've put 100 there, and
then we would've gotten 500.

00:02:57.010 --> 00:02:58.980
But even if 500 was our estimate,

00:02:58.980 --> 00:03:03.023
480 still would've been the
closest to that estimate.

